Hmm, if already exited, 'exit' may have fired before listener attached. Check exitCode/signalCode first. But there's a race: process exited but event not yet emitted and exitCode still null? Node sets exitCode when 'exit' emitted. If we attach after exit, the listener never fires. To be safe: poll. Simpler:

```ts
async function waitProcessDead(cp, timeout=5000) {
  const start = Date.now();
  for (;;) {
    try { process.kill(cp.pid, 0); } catch { return; }
    if (Date.now() - start > timeout) throw new Error('进程未退出');
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 20));
  }
}
```

